 ```
 
 The selected CPT checkpoint is step 3 (0.56 pass). It was merged into the pinned base before training a fresh, single SFT adapter with L6's data, sampler, learning rate, and terminal-EOS weight. C2 step 40 is the best L10 review checkpoint; step 50 shortens sharply. C2's individual blind model-judge averages improve modestly over L6, but 45/50 direct L6 comparisons tie, and B0/CPT-only are preferred much more often on non-ties. It does not clearly beat L6 or L1, so **L10 was not promoted**; L1 remains the current `models/best.gguf` and `writer` is unchanged. The fixed50, constraint, novel20, prose, memorization, and full blind evidence are in [EXPERIMENTS.md](EXPERIMENTS.md) and `corpus/metadata/l10_*.json`. The runbook records execution and artifact hashes. Adapters, merged weights, raw generations, and full judge packets are retained only in ignored local `outputs/l10*`. All 194 files copied from the replacement A40 matched its SHA-256 manifest, and the pod was deleted.
+
+## L11 source-target curation preflight
+
+L11 was stopped before GPU use. The source-only rubric and cutoff were committed before any L11 generation. All 224 existing L5 train targets were scored anonymously; cutoff 8 and hard completeness/lineation/context gates left 118 numeric candidates. Manual review of the preview and replacements rejected 55 weak, incomplete, or near-duplicate passages. The reproducible curated artifact has 57 unchanged targets from 39 works, with 20 privately documented prompt-fidelity revisions. It is too small for the unchanged L6 50-step exposure: the total token count would match within 1.3%, but the set would receive 8.55 effective token passes and up to 14 draws per target. The predeclared QA limits are at least 70 targets, at least 50 source works, and at most 10 draws per target. No A40 was provisioned, no L11 adapter or blind review exists, and L1 remains the incumbent. See [L11_RUNBOOK.md](L11_RUNBOOK.md) and `corpus/metadata/l11_preflight_decision.json` for the source-only evidence and stop decision.
